<title>BRAZIL: Brazil to make $27 bln on privatizations.</title>
<headline>Brazil to make $27 bln on privatizations.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-11-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian President Fernando Henrique Cardoso's government aims to earn $27 billion in privatization receipts during its four-year term, a newspaper said.</p>
<p>The Cardoso administration has already taken in $4.8 billion in privatization receipts and hopes to raise another $22 billion by the end of Cardoso's term in two years time, O Estado de Sao Paulo said.</p>
<p>-- Simona de Logu, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 507 4151</p>
